cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite this version and identify the exact release
  and evidence artifacts used. This citation describes a research software
  artifact and does not establish scientific novelty or peer review.
type: software
title: Fuzzy Dynamics Lab
authors:
  - family-names: Balázsfalvi
    given-names: Gergő
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-17'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/gbalazsfalvi/fuzzy-dynamics-lab
url: https://github.com/gbalazsfalvi/fuzzy-dynamics-lab
abstract: >-
  Research software for finite-horizon approximation of discrete dynamical
  systems with fuzzy initial states. It separates adaptive refinement policy
  selection from independently computed numerical error bounds and includes
  exact references, replayable evidence, frozen learned ranking policies,
  saved-artifact analysis and a local Java and React workbench. Certificates,
  observed errors, empirical comparisons and unresolved novelty questions
  have distinct scopes. Membership grades are not probabilities.
keywords:
  - fuzzy dynamical systems
  - interval arithmetic
  - adaptive refinement
  - reproducible research
  - numerical error bounds
